skill: "customer-health-score"
sections[3]:
  - "# customer-health-score\n\nDefine, validate and operate the composite customer health score with intervention triggers. Use when customer success needs a ranked at-risk list, after a quarter closes (to validate the score against actual churn), or when triggers fire so the right playbook reaches the right CSM owner.\n\nOwner: role-churn-analyst (pod-customer, customer_success). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"usage and engagement signals export; support ticket data; billing status from billing-automation; score config health-score-config.toon\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/customer/health-score-config.toon (signals, weights, tiers, triggers); at-risk-list.toon with per-account score, tier and assigned playbook\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load the current config; a config without a last_validated date older than one quarter is stale and must be revalidated before scores are published.\n2. Select signals from the four families: product usage, engagement, support friction and billing status; every signal must have a data source that exists today, not one planned.\n3. Normalize each signal to 0-100 with the documented direction (higher is healthier) and record the normalization rule per signal.\n4. Set weights per signal family; verify with run_command that weights sum to 100 and that no single signal exceeds the policy cap.\n5. Validate: score the last closed quarter's accounts and check that the score's churners rank above the survivors in a simple lift table; a score that does not separate churners from survivors is rejected, not shipped.\n6. Define tiers with explicit cut points and one playbook per tier; triggers name the CSM action and its due window in days.\n7. Publish the weekly at-risk-list.toon with per-account score, tier and trigger fired; accounts with data gaps get a data_gap flag instead of a fake neutral score.\n8. Log every intervention back against the account so the next validation can measure whether the playbook actually moved retention.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nat-risk list to CSM owners; validation results to retention-cohorts.\n"
